    "result_text": "All green. The implementation is complete and the build passes. Here's a summary of what I changed to release version 2 of the owner identity.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (drives DTO generation)\n- Removed the top-level `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey` from `Owner`.\n- Added a nested `identity` property (referencing a new `Identity` schema holding those three) and a top-level integer `apiVersion`.\n- Added the `Identity` schema and documented the V2 derivations.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** (owner response shape + identity derivation)\n- Added `apiVersion()` \u2192 `2` and `identity(owner)` building the nested `IdentityDto` (memberId, identityKey, householdId); dropped the old top-level householdId/identityKey mappings.\n- `identityKey` and `householdId` now mix the fixed `V2` tag into their SHA-256 inputs (`\"V2|\"` prefix), so both change and never reproduce a V1 value.\n- `locality` and `fiscalYear` now strip a leading `V2` tag from the memberId before parsing, so the **user-facing `locality` stays the plain region** (e.g. `NSW`) \u2014 and `timezone`/`ownerSegment`, which derive from it, likewise stay plain. Legacy owners (no memberId) still yield `UNKNOWN`.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** (memberId + audit)\n- `memberId` region is now prefixed with the `V2` tag (`V2NSW\u2026`) and the `HASH8` input mixes in the tag, so the identifier fully changes while the segment stays parseable back to the plain region.\n- The structured audit event moved to schema version 2, adding a `schemaVersion` field of `2`; its `memberId` is the recomputed version-2 identity.\n\n## Verification\n- `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n- Runtime audit line confirms both the V2 identifier and the new schema field: `{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW27169701686\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n- Generated `OwnerDto` now exposes `apiVersion` + `identity` (with no top-level identifier fields); `IdentityDto` holds `memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId`.\n\nThe `V2` tag appears only inside the identifiers; `locality`, `timezone`, and the owner segment's derived region remain the plain region code, and request fields are unchanged.",
