    "probe_text": "The report matches the code exactly. Here is the complete, ordered chain for **POST /api/owners** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`).\n\n## A. Before the controller runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. *(Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; the default `application.properties` sets it to `false`, so at normal runtime it's a no-op \u2014 it is enforced in tests.)*\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`) \u2014 checked before the method body; failures \u2192 400 via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/`'`/`-`-separated parts)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `title`: `@Size(max 10)`\n   - `address`: `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` non-blank\n   - `addressLine1`: `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` non-blank\n   - `addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` non-blank\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` non-blank (loose; strict E.164 comes later in the controller)\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n\n## B. Inside the controller (in execution order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 if a non-blank `Idempotency-Key` header matches a prior successful create, return that existing owner with **200 OK** (no new create).\n4. **Email** \u2014 `normalizeEmail()`: validate/normalize the optional email (includes a disposable-domain blocklist); invalid \u2192 **400**.\n5. **Postcode** \u2014 `normalizePostcode()`: validate/normalize the optional postcode against the city; invalid \u2192 **400**.\n6. **Address** \u2014 `normalizeAddresses()`: normalize `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (or flat `address`), writing the composed/normalized form back onto the DTO; none supplied \u2192 **400**.\n7. **City-capacity hard limit** \u2014 `countOwnersInCity(city)` \u2265 50 \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n8. **Telephone** \u2014 `toE164()`: normalize to E.164; invalid \u2192 **400**; normalized value written back to the DTO.\n9. **Identity-duplicate check** \u2014 map DTO\u2192`Owner`, compute `identityKey` (SHA-256 of `telephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`), scan all non-deleted owners; collision \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n10. **Registration date** \u2014 default to `LocalDate.now()` if absent; a future date \u2192 **400**; then roll weekend/holiday forward to the next business day (`toBusinessDay()`).\n11. **Daily sign-up limit** \u2014 `countOwnersRegisteredOn(adjustedDate)` \u2265 100 \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n\n## C. Side-effects \u2014 derived fields set on the entity (order as written)\n\n12. `registrationDate` \u2190 adjusted business day.\n13. `memberId` \u2190 `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (region from postcode/city, two-digit fiscal year, 8 hex of SHA-256 of telephone+lastName, Luhn check digit).\n14. `namesakeCount` \u2190 count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n15. `bulkSignupWarning` \u2190 `true` if > 80 owners already registered today.\n16. `capacityWarning` \u2190 `true` if city held 40\u201349 owners.\n17. `householdSize` \u2190 existing household members + 1.\n18. `membershipLevelCap` \u2190 one above the max membership level of existing household members (null if none).\n19. **Soft-duplicate flags** \u2014 `findPossibleDuplicate()` (same Soundex last name + postcode, distinct identity key); if the request set `sharesHousehold=true` it's an acknowledged member \u2192 not flagged; otherwise set `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n\n## D. Persist and post-persist side-effects\n\n20. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `@Transactional` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save()` (Spring Data JPA `persist`). *(No `@PrePersist`/lifecycle callbacks, no JPA auditing, and the `Owner` entity's own `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints are not re-validated here.)*\n21. **Audit log (plain)** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=\u2026 memberId=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026\")`.\n22. **Audit log (structured event)** \u2014 build `OwnerCreatedEvent` (incremented `AUDIT_SEQ`, schema version, id, primary identifier, membership level) and log it as JSON.\n23. **Notification** \u2014 `NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id=\u2026 memberId=\u2026\")`.\n24. **Record idempotency key** \u2014 store `key \u2192 owner.id` for future repeats.\n25. **Response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n**Notes:** All business rejections (400/409/429) are thrown as `RestRejectionException` and rendered as RFC 7807 `application/problem+json` by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. No custom `ConstraintValidator` is involved in this path. Steps 7, 9, 11 (and the various count helpers) each load all owners into memory via `findAllOwners()`."
